=== PARITY ===
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reads / queries (2/2 ported):
  [x] useTrips
        endpoint : GET /trips        (versioned client adds /api/v1)
        params   : vehicle_id=<id>  only when truthy (non-null AND != 0)
                   limit=<n>         only when truthy (non-null AND != 0)
                   offset=<n>        only when (!= null AND > 0)
                   start=<iso>       only when non-null AND non-blank
                   end=<iso>         only when non-null AND non-blank
                   (URLSearchParams insertion order: vehicle_id,limit,offset,start,end)
        derivation: select:safeArray → applied once at the data layer
        cache key: tripsListKey(params) ≡ web ['trips', params]
                   (TanStack hashKey: undefined dropped, 0/"" kept, sorted keys)
        staleTime: none declared → QueryClient default 60s → CacheDomain.Trips 60s TTL
        decode   : List<Trip> (SI: total_distance_m / _energy_wh / _duration_s)
  [x] useTrip
        endpoint : GET /trips/{id}   (versioned client adds /api/v1)
        params   : (none — id is a path segment)
        cache key: tripDetailKey(id) ≡ web ['trips', id]
        enabled  : web `enabled: !!id` is a render-layer gate (screen does not
                   collect trip(id) until it has an id) — NOT reproduced here
        note     : backend registers only GET /trips (no /trips/{id}); the web
                   hook is @deprecated and 404s. The 404 surfaces through
                   Resource.Error — the same channel web TripDetailPage renders
                   gracefully. Behaviour ported verbatim (no scope narrowing).
        decode   : Trip

Mutations / actions (0/0):
  (none — web hook file is read-only; no invalidation surface)

Refresh surface:
  TripsStore.refresh() ≡ web invalidateQueries({ queryKey: tripKeys.all }) — the
  ['trips'] family prefix matches BOTH the list and the detail (tripsKeyInFamily),
  re-collecting every observed feed. A feed nobody observes is a no-op.

Client-side derivations golden-pinned (KMP+C# parity, ADR-004):
  tripsQuery     — 6 vectors (all-absent / 0-dropped / offset-0-dropped /
                   blank-range-dropped / offset-present / full) + insertion-order test
  tripsListKey   — bare family / single field / full sorted / 0-and-""-kept / empty-string
  tripDetailKey  — numeric + non-numeric id, list/detail non-collision
  tripsKeyInFamily — ['trips'] matches list+detail, rejects foreign + 'trips-…' siblings

Notes / honest scope:
  - Timestamps (start_date/started_at/created_at + nullable end_date/ended_at) are
    carried as raw RFC3339 strings exactly as the web `Trip` interface types them
    (`string`); parse/format is the render boundary's job (S5).
  - SI columns round-trip verbatim; no conversion at this layer (Phase-48).
  - List + detail share CacheDomain.Trips under distinct keys; logout clears both.
  - The Trip DTO mirrors the backend tripSummaryResponse (internal/api/trip/handler.go)
    which is a superset of models.Trip — the web interface is the contract.

